WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.112
Place these names at different levels.

2
00:00:03.112 --> 00:00:09.336
RISC-V is an instruction-set architecture: it defines instructions and their

3
00:00:09.336 --> 00:00:11.465
software-visible behavior.

4
00:00:11.465 --> 00:00:15.724
OpenHW organizes collaboration around open hardware,

5
00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:21.047
and CORE-V is its portfolio of open cores and companion projects.

6
00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:25.470
CVA6 is one processor-core family implementing RISC-V.

7
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:31.038
Following the diagram, parameters define a particular configuration;

8
00:00:31.038 --> 00:00:35.788
platform hardware and software then turn it into a system.

9
00:00:35.788 --> 00:00:42.504
CV64A6 evolved from Ariane, developed at ETH Zürich and the University of Bologna.

10
00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:44.224
RV32 was added later.

11
00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:51.103
The ISA, portfolio, core and development board therefore describe different objects.

12
00:00:51.103 --> 00:00:57.982
The Foundation and CORE-V naming courses provide more background on the organization

13
00:00:57.982 --> 00:00:59.620
and its terminology.

